WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:55.510
<b>I Made It Here</b>

3
00:01:58.730 --> 00:02:04.280
The long battle that divided Skypiea
for 400 years has finally ended.

4
00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:08.480
Where there was once was war,
there is now a joyous celebration.

5
00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:11.110
No. No thanks.

6
00:02:11.110 --> 00:02:12.610
I can't drink any more.

7
00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:18.700
Great! There they are!

8
00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:24.670
Hey.

9
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:28.540
What?

10
00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.210
Go wake everyone up! Quick!

11
00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:31.630
Huh?

12
00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:32.970
But why?

13
00:02:35.170 --> 00:02:38.420
Shh! 'Cause we're gonna
steal the gold and run!

14
00:02:39.140 --> 00:02:40.470
There's gold? Where?

15
00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.470
Hey! Quiet, loudmouth!

16
00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:43.680
"Loudmouth," huh?

17
00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.730
You're a whole lot
louder than me, Luffy!

18
00:02:45.730 --> 00:02:47.380
No way! Just listen to yourself!

19
00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:49.260
You know what you are, Nami? Loud!

20
00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.100
What?! You're calling me loud?

21
00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.130
You've got some nerve, you hypocrite!

22
00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:54.680
You're super loud!

23
00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:55.680
Oh, yeah?

24
00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.600
Well, you're super mega ultra-loud!

25
00:02:57.600 --> 00:02:59.100
That's why you're yelling!

26
00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:03.250
The only reason I'm yelling is so you can
hear me over your incredibly loud voice!

27
00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:06.540
Would you two shut up?
I'm trying to sleep over here!

28
00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:09.210
Usopp, why did you hit me?!

29
00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:10.670
I'm a lady!

30
00:03:10.670 --> 00:03:14.210
And ladies don't just yell with
their mouths wide open, now, do they?

31
00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:16.090
Well, your mouth's wide open right now!

32
00:03:21.400 --> 00:03:22.900
Boy, those Blue Sea people

33
00:03:24.250 --> 00:03:26.080
sure do like to party, don't they?

34
00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.630
After four days of this,
you think they'd be worn out.

35
00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:30.710
There's no way they can be human.

36
00:03:32.780 --> 00:03:34.370
He's so cool!

37
00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:38.990
So then that's the plan, guys.

38
00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:40.690
Think he's right, gang!

39
00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.980
It's not every day we get
to go to an island in the sky,

40
00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:45.490
so let's make this trip worthwhile!

41
00:03:45.490 --> 00:03:46.780
Hmm?

42
00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:49.900
Ch-Chief! We found it!

43
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:52.070
We have just found the golden bell!

44
00:03:52.420 --> 00:03:53.000
What?

45
00:03:53.220 --> 00:03:54.120
Are you serious?

46
00:03:56.490 --> 00:04:00.080
Yes. I-It's hanging off Giant Jack,
but I don't know for how long.

47
00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:01.750
We're trying to pull it up right now.

48
00:04:01.750 --> 00:04:04.830
We need every able-bodied
warrior at the western shore now!

49
00:04:04.830 --> 00:04:05.960
We need to hurry!

50
00:04:07.130 --> 00:04:08.960
Let's go! Gather the tribe!

51
00:04:26.710 --> 00:04:29.630
To the western shore!

52
00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:32.840
The belfry.

53
00:04:34.630 --> 00:04:36.130
One more time!

54
00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:38.540
One... Two...

55
00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:42.540
Heave!

56
00:05:00.760 --> 00:05:01.630
Dammit!

57
00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.390
We still need more people!

58
00:05:07.010 --> 00:05:08.770
It's the pride of Shandora!

59
00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:10.100
We can't lose it!

60
00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:12.270
We won't!

61
00:05:12.270 --> 00:05:14.480
Give it everything you've got!

62
00:05:14.480 --> 00:05:16.610
One more time!

63
00:05:53.210 --> 00:05:56.040
You call this a "rubber band"?

64
00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:58.670
Yeah, and here's a little inside
information about 'em!

65
00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:02.880
Those babies are the primary
things that took down Giant Jack!

66
00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:04.130
My word!

67
00:06:04.130 --> 00:06:07.430
And I'm the only one in
the world who has them!

68
00:06:07.430 --> 00:06:08.470
Wow!

69
00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:14.100
But wait, there's more!
Namely... Heh heh!

70
00:06:14.100 --> 00:06:16.310
This piece of metal!

71
00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:18.440
Gather 'round, folks,
and take a gander!

72
00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.860
This is no ordinary
piece of metal, nosiree!

73
00:06:20.860 --> 00:06:23.490
It came from our valiant vessel,
the Going Merry!

74
00:06:23.490 --> 00:06:27.370
It's withstood the Grand Line and
Eneru's attacks with barely a scratch!

75
00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:30.390
This here's the "King of Metal Sheets!"

76
00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:32.640
And just think: it can all be yours!

77
00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:34.830
How 'bout it? Wanna trade some
of your dials for this?

78
00:06:34.830 --> 00:06:38.590
No, not really, but I'll gladly
trade you for this rubber band!

79
00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:40.260
So will I! Got more?

80
00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.260
Me, too!

81
00:06:41.140 --> 00:06:42.220
I want three!

82
00:06:47.060 --> 00:06:48.100
Water.

83
00:06:57.810 --> 00:07:00.770
Oh, I'm so lucky!

84
00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:02.900
You sure are in a good mood, Usopp.

85
00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.570
I'm assuming your trading went well?

86
00:07:07.750 --> 00:07:09.780
Oh, yeah! And how!

87
00:07:09.780 --> 00:07:13.100
Just look at all the dials I got!

88
00:07:13.100 --> 00:07:16.910
One little press... And voila!

89
00:07:16.910 --> 00:07:18.120
Well, good for you.

90
00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:19.480
Ya mean great!

91
00:07:19.480 --> 00:07:21.800
I can do so many things with 'em!

92
00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:27.340
The ole Usopp workshop's gonna
be totally revolutionized!

93
00:07:28.720 --> 00:07:29.970
You know what?

94
00:07:29.970 --> 00:07:31.720
I could use one to store
smells in your swords!

95
00:07:31.720 --> 00:07:35.070
That way you'll smell fresh-cut
melons every time you practice!

96
00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:36.650
– Sound good?
– No thanks.

97
00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:37.820
Oh!

98
00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:41.620
Speaking of weapons, I'm gonna use these
to make Nami's Clima-Tact stronger!

99
00:07:41.620 --> 00:07:43.290
Not to mention my slingshot!

100
00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:44.620
I can't wait!

101
00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.080
So, where's everybody else, huh?

102
00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:56.790
Luffy and the others are still inside,
and Robin went off by herself.

103
00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.420
The snake's still conked out, huh?

104
00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.400
He must be really tired.

105
00:08:05.400 --> 00:08:08.440
You'd be, too, if you
danced for four days straight.

106
00:08:08.440 --> 00:08:10.650
I wonder what he was so happy about...

107
00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:12.230
Anyway, I hope they come out soon.

108
00:08:12.230 --> 00:08:14.610
When he wakes up, I don't
know how friendly he'll be.

109
00:08:14.610 --> 00:08:15.950
Huh? Who?

110
00:08:15.950 --> 00:08:17.870
This well-mannered snake?

111
00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:20.950
Easy for you to say. You didn't
see him when he was mad.

112
00:08:20.950 --> 00:08:22.030
He's dangerous.

113
00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:23.780
Who? This well-mannered snake?

114
00:08:23.780 --> 00:08:25.290
Like I said, you didn't see him.

115
00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.040
Just wait till he tries to eat you.

116
00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:28.920
You'll see what a pain he can be.

117
00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.750
Who? This well-mannered snake?

118
00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:33.000
Usopp, are you even listening to me?

119
00:08:34.080 --> 00:08:35.820
Who? This well-mannered snake?

120
00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:37.460
Fooled ya with a tone dial!

121
00:08:37.460 --> 00:08:38.840
Stop being so stupid!

122
00:08:40.300 --> 00:08:41.510
Me? Stupid?

123
00:08:41.510 --> 00:08:43.640
But you're the one
who got fooled! Ha ha!

124
00:08:44.610 --> 00:08:45.650
What the...?

125
00:08:45.650 --> 00:08:47.800
And I thought Luffy ate too much!

126
00:08:47.800 --> 00:08:49.300
Are we there yet?

127
00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.800
There! I told ya!

128
00:08:50.800 --> 00:08:52.470
Wow! Is it...?

129
00:08:52.470 --> 00:08:54.370
Yep, the real deal!

130
00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:55.600
It's a bell!

131
00:08:55.600 --> 00:08:58.100
Just like the ones the
big monkeys showed us!

132
00:08:59.730 --> 00:09:01.520
See? See? See?

133
00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:03.980
There's so much stuff!

134
00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.440
And it's all ours!

135
00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:16.370
So, that's it.

136
00:09:16.370 --> 00:09:17.460
Amazing.

137
00:09:17.460 --> 00:09:18.750
It's beautiful.

138
00:09:18.750 --> 00:09:21.000
I didn't expect it to be so big!

139
00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.590
It's magnificent!

140
00:09:22.590 --> 00:09:25.900
Oh, but look, one of
the side columns is broken off.

141
00:09:25.900 --> 00:09:27.900
Yeah. What a shame.

142
00:09:27.900 --> 00:09:29.690
Hey, look!

143
00:09:29.690 --> 00:09:32.320
Over there! Under the bell!

144
00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.240
The Poneglyph.

145
00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:36.280
That thing?

146
00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.630
So that's the stone our ancestors
gave their lives to protect?

147
00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:43.400
Chief, the words
that are inscribed on it.

148
00:09:43.400 --> 00:09:45.520
What do they say?

149
00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:47.280
It's an ancient text.

150
00:09:50.900 --> 00:09:52.820
Impossible to read.

151
00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:55.370
"We shall know the true meaning
and utter it to no one."

152
00:09:56.770 --> 00:09:59.230
"It's our legacy to
be the inheritors of history,

153
00:09:59.620 --> 00:10:01.710
and our duty to protect it with
the sounding of the grand belfry."

154
00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:05.510
Th-Those words!

155
00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:07.090
How do you know them?

156
00:10:07.090 --> 00:10:09.760
They were inscribed on
a wall in the ruins of Shandora.

157
00:10:09.760 --> 00:10:13.430
Generations ago, your people were
entrusted to be its guardians, correct?

158
00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:22.740
You can actually read
those ancient characters?

159
00:10:28.150 --> 00:10:32.030
It mentions Poseidon,
an ancient weapon named after a god.

160
00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.580
It even gives its whereabouts.

161
00:10:33.580 --> 00:10:34.500
Are you certain?

162
00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:37.050
Ancient weapon?

163
00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:39.700
But why would it say
something like that?

164
00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:41.050
How odd.

165
00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:41.950
Yeah.

166
00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:43.630
Another weapon.

167
00:10:44.150 --> 00:10:46.690
One different from Pluton of Alabasta.

168
00:10:48.490 --> 00:10:50.490
And to think there are
dangerous things like this

169
00:10:50.490 --> 00:10:51.190
out there in

170
00:10:53.830 --> 00:10:56.000
Just another dead end.

171
00:10:56.360 --> 00:10:59.240
This isn't what I was looking
for or what I wanted to know.

172
00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:01.090
Uh, hey, Miss?

173
00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.810
Is that stuff engraved on the
side part of the Poneglyph, too?

174
00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:12.110
Gol D. Roger!

175
00:11:12.980 --> 00:11:14.900
What?

176
00:11:16.110 --> 00:11:19.070
I made it here,
and I will guide this passage

177
00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:21.610
all the way to the farthest
ends of the earth.

178
00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:24.120
The stormiest seas will not stop me.

179
00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.790
Pirate Gold Roger.

180
00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.540
The Pirate King?

181
00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:34.010
Then this could only mean that
he came to the sky islands!

182
00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:41.100
And more importantly, how was he able
to understand and use this ancient language?

183
00:11:41.610 --> 00:11:44.150
So it says "Roger," does it?

184
00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.280
You know him?

185
00:11:45.280 --> 00:11:46.410
Ah, yes.

186
00:11:46.410 --> 00:11:48.030
A Blue Sea pirate.

187
00:11:48.030 --> 00:11:51.930
I met him when he came to this
land over 20 years ago.

188
00:11:51.930 --> 00:11:54.160
I take it that his name
is inscribed there?

189
00:11:54.160 --> 00:11:55.330
Yes.

190
00:11:56.020 --> 00:12:01.110
Honestly, I have no idea how he managed
to reach this bell, but somehow he did.

191
00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:03.670
And this inscription is
proof that he was here.

192
00:12:03.670 --> 00:12:04.800
Wait a minute.

193
00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:11.560
Now that I think about it, there
are two kinds of Poneglyph stones:

194
00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:15.850
ones that contain information, and others
that tell how to reach other Poneglyphs

195
00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:17.140
scattered throughout the world.

196
00:12:19.520 --> 00:12:21.690
This stone obviously has information.

197
00:12:23.690 --> 00:12:26.190
"I made it here, and I
will guide this passage

198
00:12:26.190 --> 00:12:28.450
all the way to the farthest
ends of the earth."

199
00:12:30.450 --> 00:12:33.240
Guide this passage.

200
00:12:33.520 --> 00:12:34.780
Guide.

201
00:12:39.320 --> 00:12:40.490
Could he...

202
00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:42.450
Could he mean the Rio Poneglyph?

203
00:12:50.280 --> 00:12:51.770
Chief. This Poneglyph.

204
00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:53.940
Its duty has been fulfilled.

205
00:12:53.940 --> 00:12:55.100
Its duty?

206
00:12:57.070 --> 00:12:59.610
Yes. I have a hunch
about these Poneglyphs.

207
00:12:59.610 --> 00:13:03.700
As I said, there are certain ones spread
across the world that contain information.

208
00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:05.580
By reading them as one,
I believe they'll form

209
00:13:05.580 --> 00:13:09.730
a passage that will reveal the true
history of the Blank Century.

210
00:13:09.730 --> 00:13:14.360
In other words, the passage completed
by connecting them is what will make up

211
00:13:14.360 --> 00:13:18.450
a legendary final Poneglyph
that's yet to be discovered.

212
00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:21.210
The Rio Poneglyph.

213
00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:25.550
Gol D. Roger must have taken the text
from the Poneglyph here to the island

214
00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:28.260
where the Rio Poneglyph
may very well be located.

215
00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:35.100
He must have...

216
00:13:35.100 --> 00:13:37.060
Does that...

217
00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:43.470
Does that mean we... don't
have to fight any longer?

218
00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:50.890
Then our ancestors'
wish has been fulfilled?

219
00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:53.890
– Chief!
– Hang on!

220
00:13:53.890 --> 00:13:55.310
Are you all right?

221
00:13:55.310 --> 00:13:59.270
Thank goodness!
Our war is finally over!

222
00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:06.590
Well, I'd better
get to fulfilling my duty.

223
00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:10.900
Like Roger before me, I have to guide this
passage, and the other ones I've read,

224
00:14:10.900 --> 00:14:14.450
all the way to the end of the Grand
Line, to the island of Raftel.

225
00:14:15.930 --> 00:14:17.930
Well, then. Where were we?

226
00:14:17.930 --> 00:14:19.310
Ah, yes.

227
00:14:19.310 --> 00:14:24.810
I was about to tell you how much your
friend in the straw hat reminds me of Roger.

228
00:14:24.810 --> 00:14:27.770
That boy is... interesting.

229
00:14:27.770 --> 00:14:30.270
His name's Monkey D. Luffy.

230
00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.530
And I find him interesting as well.

231
00:14:32.530 --> 00:14:36.700
D? So the lad even shares the
same middle initial as Roger?

232
00:14:39.710 --> 00:14:41.170
Yes.

233
00:14:41.170 --> 00:14:44.290
And I'm sure there's got to be some
historical significance to that.

234
00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:46.850
Pardon me, Miss.

235
00:14:46.850 --> 00:14:50.140
But I recall you and your friends
saying that you sought gold.

236
00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:53.830
And didn't you say it was more
valuable than Vearth on the Blue Sea?

237
00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:54.710
Yes.

238
00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:59.350
We obviously can't offer you the belfry,
but how about the broken support?

239
00:14:59.350 --> 00:15:00.530
That's a great idea!

240
00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:02.450
We have to give something
to our heroes,

241
00:15:02.450 --> 00:15:04.810
and that's a perfect token
of our appreciation!

242
00:15:04.810 --> 00:15:06.290
Please take it!

243
00:15:06.290 --> 00:15:07.460
We insist!

244
00:15:07.460 --> 00:15:10.250
Uh, thanks!
But are you sure about that?

245
00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:11.380
Uh-huh.

246
00:15:13.170 --> 00:15:14.670
All right, everybody!

247
00:15:14.670 --> 00:15:17.800
Let's bring this gift to our
friends from the Blue Sea!

248
00:15:17.800 --> 00:15:19.800
If we wrap it up,
it'll be easier to carry!

249
00:15:19.800 --> 00:15:21.760
It's gonna take
every one of us to move it!

250
00:15:21.760 --> 00:15:23.470
Yeah, you're not kidding.

251
00:15:30.940 --> 00:15:32.560
Come on, Robin.

252
00:15:32.560 --> 00:15:34.190
We can't wait too long.

253
00:15:35.690 --> 00:15:37.530
I'm so hungry.

254
00:15:39.820 --> 00:15:41.530
There's not a soul in site.

255
00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:43.620
I've gotta admit, this is pretty weird.

256
00:15:43.620 --> 00:15:47.580
Wonder where all those angels
and warriors ran off to, and why.

257
00:15:47.580 --> 00:15:49.370
Hey, be thankful they're gone!

258
00:15:49.370 --> 00:15:51.500
Trust me, if they see us
making a run for it

259
00:15:51.500 --> 00:15:54.130
with all the loot we pulled
from their favorite giant snake,

260
00:15:54.130 --> 00:15:55.790
well they're not gonna be too thrilled!

261
00:15:55.790 --> 00:15:57.590
Nami and Conis probably
already have the ship

262
00:15:57.590 --> 00:16:01.670
ready to sail by now, so Robin better
hurry and get back here quick! We gotta go!

263
00:16:01.670 --> 00:16:02.970
I'm hungry, Sanji.

264
00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:04.130
Got anything to eat?

265
00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:05.490
Nope. All the food's on the ship.

266
00:16:06.470 --> 00:16:09.090
You've gotta have
something to munch on, right?

267
00:16:09.090 --> 00:16:11.010
– Come on, gimme something!
– I've had enough!

268
00:16:11.010 --> 00:16:12.810
I'm tired of just sittin' around.

269
00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:15.060
You guys can wait for her.
I'm gonna go to the ship.

270
00:16:15.060 --> 00:16:16.230
Moron!

271
00:16:16.230 --> 00:16:17.190
Jerk!

272
00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:18.150
What are you?

273
00:16:18.150 --> 00:16:19.520
Stupid head!

274
00:16:28.430 --> 00:16:29.720
Hey, look! It's Robin!

275
00:16:31.370 --> 00:16:32.950
Hi, hot stuff!

276
00:16:32.950 --> 00:16:35.080
Hey! Robin!

277
00:16:35.080 --> 00:16:37.420
Hurry up! Run!

278
00:16:37.420 --> 00:16:38.790
We've gotta leave!

279
00:16:38.790 --> 00:16:40.420
We stole some gold!

280
00:16:40.420 --> 00:16:43.550
Stop it! Look, you moron!

281
00:16:43.550 --> 00:16:46.430
Right behind her! See them?
They can hear you, too!

282
00:16:46.430 --> 00:16:48.930
It's an army!

283
00:16:50.680 --> 00:16:54.030
Oh, no! Not good! Not good!

284
00:16:55.450 --> 00:16:57.160
That big thing can only be one thing!

285
00:16:57.160 --> 00:16:57.910
What?

286
00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.940
A cannon!

287
00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:03.230
Just our luck they'd
all come back at once.

288
00:17:04.040 --> 00:17:06.410
Robin! Get the lead out!

289
00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:09.830
We've gotta get back to the ship now!

290
00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:11.570
Check out this gold!

291
00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:14.630
I bet we found every
piece on the island, huh?

292
00:17:14.630 --> 00:17:17.430
From here, it looks like they've
already packed their bags!

293
00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:20.390
Oh, no! They're not leaving already!

294
00:17:20.390 --> 00:17:21.850
Hold on, you guys!

295
00:17:21.850 --> 00:17:23.060
Don't go!

296
00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:25.390
Oh, great! Here they come!

297
00:17:25.390 --> 00:17:26.550
Run!

298
00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:29.470
Well, I guess it's up
to me to handle this one.

299
00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:33.610
Stop? Stop, you say?

300
00:17:33.610 --> 00:17:34.850
Like hell we'll stop!

301
00:17:34.850 --> 00:17:36.810
Yeah! You tell 'em, Usopp!

302
00:17:38.290 --> 00:17:41.290
We risked life and limb
to come to this island

303
00:17:40.350 --> 00:17:41.820
– in the sky!
– Yeah, we did!

304
00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:44.040
And then we found the city of gold!

305
00:17:44.280 --> 00:17:50.210
So you think we pirates are leaving
empty-handed, you've got another thing coming!

306
00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:52.080
Capture them? What's he talking about?

307
00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:54.470
The only thing we're trying
to do is thank them!

308
00:17:54.540 --> 00:17:56.300
Uh, Miss, is there a problem?

309
00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:58.590
You and your friends
want this gold, right?

310
00:18:01.940 --> 00:18:03.040
I guess we don't!

311
00:18:03.040 --> 00:18:04.590
– What?
– What?

312
00:18:04.590 --> 00:18:06.460
Please wait!

313
00:18:09.590 --> 00:18:13.970
Let's go!

314
00:18:13.970 --> 00:18:15.350
I can't turn around!

315
00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:17.560
I know they're chasing us!

316
00:18:17.560 --> 00:18:20.560
Zoro, didja see
me take care of 'em back there?

317
00:18:20.560 --> 00:18:23.760
Yeah! Not bad!

318
00:18:23.760 --> 00:18:26.640
Hey, Robin! Better hurry up!

319
00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:29.760
– Hey! Come back! Wait!
– Hey! Come back! Wait!

320
00:18:30.020 --> 00:18:35.480
Don't stop until we reach Cloud End!

321
00:18:35.480 --> 00:18:37.070
– Aye!
– Aye!

322
00:18:42.750 --> 00:18:48.270
When you're lost and alone, call out and lead me to your side

323
00:18:48.490 --> 00:18:53.690
As you wander far from home, you search the sky and never hide

324
00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.490
You are so much like the moon

325
00:18:56.490 --> 00:19:01.140
Calmer than a star, your twinkling's lost

326
00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:13.540
A deep reflection shines, you slowly leave, fading, and what's the cost?

327
00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:18.770
Stay as you are, don't lose your way

328
00:19:18.770 --> 00:19:27.080
Let my words guide you, and look ahead until the day!

329
00:19:27.720 --> 00:19:33.970
Don't give up on your dreams, through endless nights they come to you

330
00:19:33.970 --> 00:19:39.590
If you stop, you'll never see them shining through!

331
00:19:40.830 --> 00:19:45.360
Will you return? Maybe not... Will you learn? I hope you do

332
00:19:45.360 --> 00:19:51.750
Please put your past to rest, and live your life anew.
